  "raw_sections": {
    "personal_information": "RUSHI M\nBusiness Analyst / Technical Project Analyst Bengaluru, Karnataka, India +91-9632100124 | rushimupalla@gmail.com linkedin.com/in/rushimuppalla",
    "summary": "PROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nResults-oriented Business Analyst with 4+ years of experience across requirements documentation, QA coordination, change management, and stakeholder communication in Agile and hybrid delivery environments. Strong hands-on exposure to BRD, SRS, user stories, UAT planning, regression coordination, and production issue analysis. Experienced in client-facing roles requiring documentation discipline, traceability, and controlled change delivery.",
    "skills": "CORE SKILLS\nRequirements Gathering (BRD, FRD, SRS) • Manual Testing and QA Process • Requirement Traceability Matrix • Change Request and Impact Analysis • User Stories and Acceptance Criteria • UAT Planning and Execution • Regression Testing and Release • Client Stake Holder Management • Root Cause Analysis\nTOOLS & TECHNOLOGIES\nJira, SQL Server, MS Office, Figma, Snagit, Linux, Power BI",
    "experience": "PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nTechnical Project Analyst\nIQVIA | Sep 2023 – February 2026\nAct as a client-facing analyst for customization of IRT applications in global clinical trials.\nOwn requirement clarification, documentation, and validation across IT, Business, and external stakeholders.\nManage Software Change Requests (SCRs) including scope definition, feasibility checks, and impact analysis.\nPrepare and review UAT plans, scenarios, and test cases aligned with client-specific guidelines.\nCoordinate UAT execution, issue tracking, defect triage, and resolution with cross- functional teams.\nValidate fixes and enhancements to ensure release readiness and quality compliance. • Support production issue analysis, documentation, and corrective actions.\nDevelop training materials, SOPs, and user documentation for internal and external users.\nMaintain effective communication with internal teams and client stakeholders throughout delivery cycles.\nBusiness Analyst\nLOYLTWO3KS IT Pvt. Ltd. | Jul 2021 – Sep 2023\nOwned end-to-end requirement gathering for small to mid-scale product enhancements, bug fixes, and CRs.\nCreated and maintained BRD, SRS, user stories, acceptance criteria, workflows, and validation rules.\nConducted GAP analysis, feasibility studies, and detailed impact analysis before development start.\nActed as the single point of contact between clients, product, QA, and development teams.\nSupported manual testing activities, reviewed test cases, and validated test results. • Prepared release notes, user manuals, FAQs, and training documentation. • Supported clients during production issues, performed RCA, and ensured resolution closure.\nAssisted in defining QA and documentation best practices within Agile (Scrum) framework and Waterfall methodologies.",
    "education": "EDUCATION\nBachelor of Engineering (Civil Engineering) Sri Venkateshwara College of Engineering, VTU"
  },
